  "details": "**Description:**\n\nThere is a synchronization bug when using the Camera Dolly's Multi-Streaming mode with the `IsLocal` setting. When multiple paths are active, only the first camera updates its relative position to the moving player in real-time. The other cameras do not track the player's movement in real-time and instead snap/teleport to the accumulated distance only when their path animation loops or ends.\n\n**Important Note:** This is not a performance/rendering lag issue with 4 cameras. **This exact same bug happens even when testing with only 2 paths.**\n\n**Steps to Reproduce:**\n\n1. Open Camera Dolly and enable **Multi-Streaming** mode.\n\n2. Create **2 Paths** (Path 1 and Path 2).\n\n3. Set both paths to **`IsLocal`** so they should follow the player's movement.\n\n4. Hit Play and physically move your avatar around.\n\n5. Look at the Spout outputs.\n\n**Expected Behavior:**\n\nBoth Spout outputs (Camera 1 and Camera 2) should follow the player's movement smoothly in real-time based on their respective animations.\n\n**Actual Behavior:**\n\n* Camera 1 (Path 1) follows the player's local position perfectly in real-time.\n\n* Camera 2 (Path 2) ignores the player's movement and stays at the starting coordinate playing its animation. When its animation finishes/loops, Camera 2 suddenly SNAPS(teleports) to catch up with the player's current location all at once.\n\nIt seems the Transform update loop for the player's local position is missing or disconnected for all additional cameras (Path 2, 3, and 4) in Multi-Stream mode.",
